1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,388
A display driver gives the shape of a part or a field a default place.

2
00:00:05,388 --> 00:00:09,083
A placement file changes that place without touching code.

3
00:00:09,083 --> 00:00:13,124
This video shows the file format, how to target a shape, and how

4
00:00:13,124 --> 00:00:15,260
to move, hide and group shapes.

5
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:23,527
A display driver builds a shape for a part or a field, and

6
00:00:23,527 --> 00:00:25,476
gives it a default location:

7
00:00:25,476 --> 00:00:27,768
a zone, and optionally a position.

8
00:00:27,768 --> 00:00:33,040
This text field driver uses the Content zone for the Detail and Summary display types.

9
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:36,369
A placement file overrides that default.

10
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:40,350
It moves a shape to another zone or position, hides it, or groups

11
00:00:40,350 --> 00:00:42,481
it into tabs, cards and columns.

12
00:00:42,481 --> 00:00:46,630
It works for the front end and for the content editors of the admin.

13
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:52,203
A rule finds a shape by its shape type, its differentiator and its display type.

14
00:00:52,203 --> 00:00:56,017
It can also look at the content item the shape was built from,

15
00:00:56,017 --> 00:00:57,700
and at the request path.

16
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:06,497
Any module or theme can contain a placement.json file at its root, and

17
00:01:06,497 --> 00:01:09,279
so can the startup project of your site.

18
00:01:09,279 --> 00:01:12,969
The file is an object whose properties are shape types.

19
00:01:12,969 --> 00:01:15,630
Each property holds an array of rules.

20
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:20,748
A rule has two kinds of properties, and all of them are optional.

21
00:01:20,748 --> 00:01:23,577
Filters choose the shapes it applies to:

22
00:01:23,577 --> 00:01:27,822
displayType, differentiator, contentType, contentPart and path.

23
00:01:27,822 --> 00:01:31,143
Placement information says what to do with them:

24
00:01:31,143 --> 00:01:33,850
place, alternates, wrappers and shape.

25
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:39,520
The displayType and differentiator filters must equal the shape's own values.

26
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:44,558
The contentType filter accepts content types and stereotypes, and a star at the

27
00:01:44,558 --> 00:01:47,700
end matches every name starting with that text.

28
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:51,863
The contentPart filter matches items that have the part.

29
00:01:51,863 --> 00:01:55,662
The path filter matches the request path, and a star at the end

30
00:01:55,662 --> 00:01:58,360
matches every path starting with that text.

31
00:01:59,110 --> 00:02:03,090
The place property sets the location, and a dash hides the shape.

32
00:02:03,090 --> 00:02:08,190
The alternates property adds alternate shape types, and wrappers adds wrapper shapes.

33
00:02:08,190 --> 00:02:12,170
The shape property replaces the shape type with the one you name.

34
00:02:16,370 --> 00:02:21,307
A rule's property name is the shape type, and it is not always the part's name.

35
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:25,779
A part with a display driver, such as TitlePart, is a shape of its own.

36
00:02:25,779 --> 00:02:29,670
Its differentiator is the part's name, even for a named part.

37
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:34,323
A dynamic part, which has no class of its own, is displayed with

38
00:02:34,323 --> 00:02:38,616
the ContentPart shape, and the differentiator is still the part's name.

39
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:44,080
For other display types, the shape type carries the display type, as in ContentPart_Summary.

40
00:02:44,830 --> 00:02:49,296
A field is a shape named after its field type, such as TextField.

41
00:02:49,296 --> 00:02:55,208
Its differentiator is the part name, a dash, and the field name, as in Article-Subtitle.

42
00:02:55,208 --> 00:02:58,730
A content type's own part is named after the type.

43
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:05,437
Editor shapes end in Edit, such as TextField_Edit, and keep the same differentiator.

44
00:03:05,437 --> 00:03:09,938
To move or hide a whole row of the editor, label included, use

45
00:03:09,938 --> 00:03:16,160
ContentPart_Edit, with the content type, a dash and the part name as the differentiator.

46
00:03:16,910 --> 00:03:20,073
A field with a display mode needs the longer form.

47
00:03:20,073 --> 00:03:25,156
The shape type ends in Display, as in TextField_Display, and the differentiator ends

48
00:03:25,156 --> 00:03:28,770
with the full shape type, which includes the display mode.

49
00:03:32,970 --> 00:03:35,199
A place starts with a zone name.

50
00:03:35,199 --> 00:03:38,953
A colon adds a position, and a dot reaches into a zone, as

51
00:03:38,953 --> 00:03:43,879
in Parts.Article, where the editor holds the shapes of the part named Article.

52
00:03:43,879 --> 00:03:46,460
A leading slash targets a layout zone.

53
00:03:47,210 --> 00:03:49,474
Positions compare as numbers:

54
00:03:49,474 --> 00:03:54,133
two comes before ten, and one point five fits between one and two.

55
00:03:54,133 --> 00:03:58,467
Before and after mark the ends; start and end go beyond them.

56
00:03:58,467 --> 00:04:03,190
No position counts as zero, or as the part's position in an editor.

57
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:06,951
In the editor, a place can also name groups.

58
00:04:06,951 --> 00:04:11,047
A hash adds a tab, a percent sign a card, and a pipe a column.

59
00:04:11,047 --> 00:04:17,070
A semicolon after the name sets the group's position, and an underscore sets a column's width.

60
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:22,038
These rules put a media field in a tab named Media, shown first,

61
00:04:22,038 --> 00:04:25,473
and an HTML field in the Content tab, shown second.

62
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:28,486
Shapes without a group join the Content tab.

63
00:04:28,486 --> 00:04:31,740
Tabs can hold cards, and cards can hold columns.

64
00:04:32,490 --> 00:04:37,081
In a display driver, the Location method also takes a fluent builder.

65
00:04:37,081 --> 00:04:41,488
Zone, Tab, Card and Column chain on one builder, and the result is

66
00:04:41,488 --> 00:04:44,610
the string you would otherwise write by hand.

67
00:04:48,828 --> 00:04:52,981
This is the editor of an Article, before the startup project of the

68
00:04:52,981 --> 00:04:54,802
site has a placement file.

69
00:04:54,802 --> 00:04:58,273
The Title comes first, then the Permalink and the body.

70
00:04:58,273 --> 00:05:01,118
The Subtitle and the Banner Image come last.

71
00:05:01,570 --> 00:05:07,259
The Subtitle is a TextField named Subtitle, so its editor shape is TextField_Edit

72
00:05:07,259 --> 00:05:10,332
with the differentiator Article-Subtitle.

73
00:05:10,332 --> 00:05:17,460
The Banner Image is a MediaField named Image, so its differentiator is Article-Image, not Banner Image.

74
00:05:19,060 --> 00:05:22,790
The startup project of the site holds this placement.json.

75
00:05:22,790 --> 00:05:27,104
The first rule moves the Subtitle to position zero point five of the

76
00:05:27,104 --> 00:05:30,252
Parts zone, between the Title and the Permalink.

77
00:05:30,252 --> 00:05:33,750
The second puts the Banner Image in a tab named Media.

78
00:05:35,354 --> 00:05:39,899
With the file in place, the same editor has two tabs, Content and Media.

79
00:05:39,899 --> 00:05:44,676
The Subtitle sits directly under the Title, because a position of zero point

80
00:05:44,676 --> 00:05:47,764
five falls between the Title and the Permalink.

81
00:05:48,216 --> 00:05:50,711
The Banner Image has left the Content tab.

82
00:05:50,711 --> 00:05:53,206
Opening the Media tab shows it on its own.

83
00:05:57,406 --> 00:06:02,388
When several placement files place the same shape, the startup project wins, then

84
00:06:02,388 --> 00:06:04,735
the active theme, then the modules.

85
00:06:04,735 --> 00:06:07,713
A module that depends on another wins over it.

86
00:06:07,713 --> 00:06:12,236
The active theme is the front end theme, or the admin theme in the admin.

87
00:06:12,986 --> 00:06:17,658
Inside one file, when several rules match a shape, the last one wins.

88
00:06:17,658 --> 00:06:22,517
A property that placement does not know, such as a misspelled filter, is

89
00:06:22,517 --> 00:06:26,566
ignored, so the rule matches more shapes than you intended.

90
00:06:28,566 --> 00:06:33,365
Placement files keep the layout of parts and fields out of your drivers and templates.

91
00:06:33,365 --> 00:06:38,060
A separate video covers the Placements module, which edits placement from the admin.

92
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:39,416
Thanks for watching.

